<title>UK: Card Clear to help Safeway fight fraud.</title>
<headline>Card Clear to help Safeway fight fraud.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Card payment and fraud prevention company Card Clear Plc said on Tuesday it had signed a three-year agreement with British supermarkets group Safeway Plc to help in the fight against payment fraud.  </p>
<p>Card Clear said in a statement its system will be installed in all of Safeway's food and fuel outlets and it estimates more than 50 million transaction will be handled in the first year.</p>
<p>The system will check any card transactions below Safeway's &quot;floor limits&quot; at all its sales points. Any transaction above the store's limits will be checked with the relevant bank or credit card agency.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
</text>
